Vikram and Betal: The Kind Prince

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a young prince who was very kind,” said Betal. “He always helped the poor and cared for others.”

One day, while traveling, the prince found an old man struggling to carry a heavy load.

The prince immediately helped him and carried the load himself.

Later, the prince found a hungry child and gave him all his food.

By the end of the day, the prince had nothing left for himself.

That night, he felt tired and hungry but was happy.

The next morning, the king heard about the prince’s actions.

He called the prince and rewarded him.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why did the prince help others even when he had little?”

Vikram replied, “Because true kindness comes from the heart, not from wealth.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Kindness is more valuable than riches.
